# GitHub resolves relative image paths in a README against the repository
# root, but Sphinx resolves them relative to docs/ because index.rst does
# `include ../README.rst`. One figure directive cannot satisfy both, so the
# paths in README.rst use the short Sphinx-relative form and the rule below
# redirects GitHub to the real directory.
#
# Note: plain git reports "not a valid attribute name" for this line, because
# git only knows `name=value` attributes and a path is not a valid name. The
# directive is a GitHub extension; the warning is expected and harmless.
docs/*.png  docs/screenshots/